"{\"len\":6685,\"text\":\"Overview\\nRules\\nDiscussion\\nMy Submissions\\nIgnyte Challenges Competition Rules\\nOne Application per Participant\\n\\nEach participant must register for the competition with a unique Ignyte Challenges account. Multiple registrations from the same participant will result in disqualification.\\n\\nNo private sharing externally\\n\\nSharing code, data, or strategies externally is prohibited. Sharing publicly in the Ignyte Challenges community forum is encouraged, provided it's available to all participants.\\n\\nSubmission Limits\\n\\nEach participant can submit a maximum of only One entry. The maximum file size for file submissions is 40MB each.\\n\\nCompetition Timeline\\n\\nThe competition timeline, including entry deadlines and final submission deadlines, is available on the Ignyte Challenges > Overview Page\\n\\nWinner License Type\\n\\nNon-exclusive License\\n\\nData Access and Use\\n\\nData may only be used for participation in this competition.\\n\\nEligibility\\n\\nParticipation and submissions are open to all\\n\\nEntry Requirements\\n\\nRegistration is a must. Submissions must comply with competition guidelines available on the Ignyte Challenges > Overview Page. Entries must be submitted before the stated deadline\\n\\nGeneral Rules\\nBinding Agreement\\n\\nBy submitting an entry, you agree to these official competition rules, which are binding.\\n\\nData and Code Requirements\\n\\nYou are allowed to use publicly available data for your submissions, but not to share data or code externally.\\n\\nAutomated Tools\\n\\nYou may use automated machine learning tools (e.g., Google AutoML, H2O, etc.), provided you hold the appropriate license.\\n\\nSubmissions\\n\\nYour submission must meet the competition's guidelines for data format, content, and methodology. Any submission that does not comply with these rules will be disqualified.\\n\\nWinner Determination\\n\\nWinners will be determined based on performance according to the evaluation metrics outlined on the competition website.\\n\\nNotification of winners & disqualification\\n\\nPotential winners will be notified via email provided.\\n\\nIf a potential winner (i) does not respond within one (1) week of the first notification attempt or (ii) declines the nomination within one week after the final submission deadline, they will forfeit the prize. In such cases, an alternate winner will be selected based on the competition's judging criteria.\\nIf a participant fails to comply with these conditions, Ignyte Challenges will disqualify them.\\nIgnyte Challenges reserves the right to disqualify any participant who attempts to undermine the competition through cheating, deception, harassment, or any other unfair practices.\\nDisqualified participants may be removed from the competition leaderboard, and associated awards like points or medals will be withheld.\\nThe final leaderboard will be publicly displayed on the Ignyte Challenges platform. Decisions made by the competition sponsor are final.\\nWinners' obligations\\n\\nTo receive the prize, winners must:\\n\\nDeliver the final solution and associated documentation used to generate the winning submission. The solution should follow specific documentation guidelines and be usable.\\nIf the submission includes commercially available software, the winner should identify it and provide details on how it can be procured.\\nGrant Ignyte Challenges the appropriate license to use the winning submission.\\nComplete all prize acceptance forms, including eligibility certifications and tax-related documents (if applicable).\\nPrizes\\nPrizes are described on the competition website and are available only during the competition period.\\nWinners will be selected based on eligible submissions and skill level. All prizes are subject to verification of eligibility and compliance with competition rules.\\nIf a submission does not comply with the rules, the sponsor can disqualify it or ask the winner to resolve issues within one week of notice.\\nIf a participant declines to be nominated as a winner, they may forfeit the prize.\\nPrize winner/s will be notified (individual/team). The applicant must submit necessary documents. The prize cannot be transferred or assigned.\\nFor team winners, the prize money will be equally distributed unless the team unanimously opts for a different distribution before the prize is issued.\\nTaxes\\nThe winner/s is/are responsible for any taxes imposed on their prize (if applicable).\\nPrize payments are subject to compliance with applicable tax laws.\\nPublicity\\nThe winner/s agree to allow the sponsor and affiliates to use their name and likeness for promotional purposes without additional compensation, unless prohibited by law.\\nPrivacy\\nBy entering the competition, participants agree that their personal data will be collected, stored, and used in accordance with the privacy policies of Ignyte Challenges. Personal data may be shared with sponsors for purposes related to the competition.\\nWarranty, indemnity and release\\nParticipants warrant that their submissions are original and do not infringe on any third-party rights.\\nParticipants agree to indemnify and hold harmless the competition sponsor and its affiliates from any claims or damages arising from their submission or participation in the competition.\\nIgnyte Challenges is not responsible for any errors related to the competition platform or submission process.\\nInternet\\n\\nThe sponsor is not responsible for any technical issues that prevent participation, including internet failures or website malfunctions.\\n\\nRight to cancel, modify or disqualify\\nIf the competition cannot proceed as planned due to technical or other issues, the sponsor reserves the right to cancel, modify, or suspend the competition.\\nAny attempt to disrupt the competition may result in disqualification.\\nNot an offer or contract of employment\\n\\nParticipation in the competition does not constitute an offer of employment with Ignyte Challenges or any of its affiliates unless explicitly stated by Ignyte.\\n\\nGoverning law\\n\\nClaims related to the competition will be governed by the laws of the country in which the sponsor is based, and disputes will be resolved in the relevant courts.\"}"